{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Memoization** is the easiest way to turn a slow recursion into DP: keep the recursive function exactly as it is, and add a **cache** (the *memo*). Before solving a subproblem, look it up; if it's there, return the stored answer at once. Otherwise solve it, store the answer, and return it. Each distinct subproblem is now solved only once. It's called **top-down** because it starts from the question you want answered and recurses down only into the subproblems it actually needs."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/6edd8766-33aa-4c24-b2a3-41fea4e0bd68.svg",
      "alt": "fib(5) with memoization. The first time down the left side computes fib(4), fib(3), fib(2), fib(1) and fib(0). When fib(4) then asks for fib(2), and fib(5) asks for fib(3), the answers are already in the memo, so those calls return immediately without recursing: 9 calls instead of 15.",
      "width": 723,
      "height": 528,
